From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 04 Sep 2026 17:22:25 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] internal/syscall/windows, os: free the name before a delete completes

Deleteat (CL 713480, Go 1.26) uses FILE_DISPOSITION_INFORMATION_EX, whose POSIX
semantics remove the name immediately. That class was added in Windows 10,
version 1607, and a file system can lack it on any Windows version. The
fallback is FILE_DISPOSITION_INFO, which only marks the file for deletion, so
the name stays in the directory until the last handle to the file is closed.
os.Remove, which deletes through DeleteFileW, has the same problem on those
kernels.

	delete a file someone holds open  ->  the name stays
	                                  ->  Stat still finds it
	                                  ->  the name cannot be reused
	                                  ->  RemoveAll: directory not empty

Rename the file out of the way before marking it for deletion. The name is then
free immediately, and the file is removed when the last handle closes, even if
the process exits first. The file goes to the temporary directory when that is
on the same volume. Otherwise it is renamed within its own directory, and
RemoveAll of that directory still fails as before.

os.Remove deletes a file from its parent directory through Deleteat first, and
lets the old calls decide the result when that fails, so that every error
stays the one they report. Windows 10, version 1607 and later take the POSIX
path there, as DeleteFileW does. Measured on Windows 7 RTM and Windows 11.

diff --git a/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go b/src/internal/syscall/windows/at_windows.go
